# Boceto fidelity

The sketch must depict the **named lift**. A coach catching a press drawn as a row is a product failure.

## Pipeline (do not weaken)

1. Classify from the **title** only (`name` + `nameEn`). Intro/purpose never change movement.
2. Press = **PUSH**. Machine press = seated machine frame, handles **up** or **forward**. Never cables, never a row.
3. Image prompt starts with **HARD LOCK**. Classified lifts omit intro/purpose.
4. Do **not** image-to-image from squat/pull-up/push-up refs for presses, machines, floor drills, or cuff work — those poses leak.
5. After generation, vision QA must reject a wrong pattern and retry once without refs.
6. Library JPG only on a strong same-family match. Press never resolves to `row` / `pullup` / `latpulldown` / `invertedrow` / `facepull`.
7. Run `npm test` after changing matching, briefs, prompts, or generation.

## Bug that must not return

`PRESS DE HOMBRO EN MAQUINA` was drawn as a seated cable row because `hombro` triggered band rotation, intro leaked into the prompt, and a hanging-pull reference copied the pose.
